    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93872" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σησᾰμ-ῆ</span></b> , ἡ, 
			contr.
		 from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σησαμέα</span> (which occurs
		in Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
			2.425
		</span></i>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a mixture of
				sesame-seeds, roasted and pounded with honey</i>, an Athenian
			delicacy, given to guests at a wedding, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				869
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				938
			</span></i>; in pl., <i><span class="en">
				Amphis
				9.3
			</span></i>; wrongly written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σησάμη</span> in
				<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Int.</u>
				42
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
